# CODEOWNERS
#
# Every file has an owner: the catch-all below means no pull request merges
# into `dev` or `main` without an approving review from the owners team. The
# specific paths after it are redundant today (same owners) but are kept so
# the sensitive areas are explicit and can be reassigned later without
# rewriting this file.
#
# Order matters: the LAST matching pattern wins, so `*` goes first.
#
# Any ONE member of a listed team satisfies the requirement -- not all of them.
#
# GitHub reads this file from the BASE branch of a pull request, so a change
# here takes effect for PRs into `dev` once merged to `dev`, and for PRs into
# `main` after the next `dev` -> `main` release merge.
#
# Listed owners must have write access to the repository for the rule to
# apply. Owners are auto-requested as reviewers on every matching PR, and on
# `main` their approval is required (Main Branch Rules -> Require review from
# Code Owners).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default owner for everything not matched more specifically below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                                       @SAGE-3/owners

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CI, automation policy, and this file itself.
# An agent that can edit its own workflow or its own rules is not gated.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/                                               @SAGE-3/owners
/AGENTS.md                                              @SAGE-3/owners

